Not at all. NetHack is actually very forgiving of mistakes as roguelikes
go; you tend not to die unless you make two or three in a row, or one
really major one. That's how the long streaks are achieved.

The #1 mistake, of course, is not stopping and thinking as soon as
something out of place happens. Whether that's an out-of-depth monster,
or dropping to lower health than you feel comfortable on, or
accidentally using the wrong item, you need to figure out what to do
next in order to resolve the situation.

